component About {
	<Head>
		<title>about — vesk</title>
		<meta name="description" content="What Vesk is: a compiler-first reactive UI framework for the post-VDOM web." />
	</Head>
	<div class="page-wrap">
		<div class="crumb">about<span class="crumb-sep">/</span>index</div>
		<h1 class="page-h1">About Vesk</h1>
		<p class="page-lede">
			Vesk is a compiler-first reactive UI framework. One <code>.vsk</code> source —
			a TypeScript superset — compiles to SSR HTML on the server and per-cell
			DOM updates in the browser.
		</p>
		<div class="claims" style="margin-top: 1.4rem;">
			<div class="claims-row">
				<div>
					<h2 class="claim-title">How it works</h2>
					<p class="claim-body">The compiler parses each <code>.vsk</code> file into a shared IR, then emits two artifacts from one pass: static HTML for the server, and targeted per-cell updates for the client. Static subtrees carry no hydration markers — and no runtime.</p>
				</div>
				<code class="claim-art">parse (.vsk) → IR → html + cells</code>
			</div>
			<div class="claims-row">
				<div>
					<h2 class="claim-title">Why it's fast</h2>
					<p class="claim-body">No virtual DOM means no reconciliation pass. Reactivity is fine-grained — <code>track()</code> cells subscribe exactly where they render, and writes flush in one microtask batch.</p>
				</div>
				<code class="claim-art">set(cell) → 1 microtask flush</code>
			</div>
			<div class="claims-row">
				<div>
					<h2 class="claim-title">What you write</h2>
					<p class="claim-body">Components, statement-mode pages, islands for the browser, or <code>{'return <jsx>'}</code> if you prefer expression mode. Both modes compile to identical output.</p>
				</div>
				<code class="claim-art">component + track + {'<style>'}</code>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div style="height: 2.5rem;"></div>
		<p class="lbl" style="margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">explore</p>
		<div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
			<Link class="btn" href="/guide">read the guide</Link>
			<Link class="btn" href="/blog">blog</Link>
			<Link class="btn" href="/statements">statement demos</Link>
		</div>
	</div>
}